                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "54c08af0-93c8-4aff-98b4-0f7731587b8d",
                        "entry_id": "fe21816c-1af9-36cf-93e3-4447365196bd",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pinmen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2ff05864-09e1-3d50-a0e9-bff36a035bbc",
                        "entry_id": "fe21816c-1af9-36cf-93e3-4447365196bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One whose job involves working with pins (any sense)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "91b0499c-bd97-454f-bf97-fbc34bae3dec",
                                "sense_id": "2ff05864-09e1-3d50-a0e9-bff36a035bbc",
                                "text": "The modern haberdasher has swallowed up the mercer, the draper, the skinner, among the ancient trades, and the hosier, the glover, the needlemaker, the pinman, and we know not how many more, among more modern trades."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aad6e38f-1923-49c8-8762-9ffdf1674bed",
                                "sense_id": "2ff05864-09e1-3d50-a0e9-bff36a035bbc",
                                "text": "The second pinman, similarly equipped, also accompanies the surveyor, and relieves the first when the pins of the latter are used up."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a70ed16-9926-46eb-aa60-f9151d1d87f9",
                                "sense_id": "2ff05864-09e1-3d50-a0e9-bff36a035bbc",
                                "text": "In substance, it was alleged that appellee and two other members of a switch crew were engaged in transferring cars from one switch track to another, and that as he was walking upon and near the end of the last car but one, the pinman, as he is designated in the testimony, without notice or warning uncoupled the last car and signaled the engineer to reverse the movement of the train, which was suddenly done, thus throwing appellee forward and off the car."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56cc6767-ea0b-4aa4-9862-bc5bbec3220f",
                                "sense_id": "2ff05864-09e1-3d50-a0e9-bff36a035bbc",
                                "text": "Of course, we sent a bunch of pretty good pinmen to Berlin in 1936 for all-out bowling war."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a4b65d9-de3d-4334-8439-bc3089a6686d",
                                "sense_id": "2ff05864-09e1-3d50-a0e9-bff36a035bbc",
                                "text": "The lay-out cat maneuvered, snorting and starting and stopping, and the pinman bobbed on and off, unhooking the wagons one by one."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c53c743-a51f-40f3-871b-e8b313c17ddb",
                                "sense_id": "2ff05864-09e1-3d50-a0e9-bff36a035bbc",
                                "text": "When the hole was drilled, the pinman slipped a 6 x 6 inch steel plate with a hole in the center over the end of a 4-foot, steel-ribbed glue pin, pushing it down to the head of the pin."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "730cec59-0db7-3dea-93db-b8ca2cc4fc1d",
                        "entry_id": "fe21816c-1af9-36cf-93e3-4447365196bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A rudimentary drawing of a figure, such as a stick figure."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "57ad0163-930d-47d2-8aab-8d547a8cd24b",
                                "sense_id": "730cec59-0db7-3dea-93db-b8ca2cc4fc1d",
                                "text": "A red pinman means wait, a green pinman means cross, and he flashes when the crossing period is ending."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82dc440f-d71a-432a-adfb-20dbe071e91a",
                                "sense_id": "730cec59-0db7-3dea-93db-b8ca2cc4fc1d",
                                "text": "Teacher divides the class into pairs and hands them cards bearing pinmen pictures showing passive actions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "59264b81-bde7-419d-b9b5-4775c938aecb",
                                "sense_id": "730cec59-0db7-3dea-93db-b8ca2cc4fc1d",
                                "text": "Here they were, tiny pinmen, on a suburban verandah, caught up in the tail of a comet 14 million miles away."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
